Question 30: Static synchronized vs Instance synchronized

25.1 Definition

There are two types of synchronized methods in Java.

Instance Synchronized Method
Locks the current object (this).

public synchronized void increment() {

}

Static Synchronized Method

Locks the Class object.

public static synchronized void print() {

}

This is the biggest interview point.

25.2 What Gets Locked?

Instance Method

public synchronized void deposit() {

}

Locks

this

Current object's monitor.

Static Method
public static synchronized void deposit() {

}

Locks

Class Object

Example

Counter.class

