25.4 Instance Synchronized Example

class Counter {
    public synchronized void increment() {
        System.out.println(Thread.currentThread().getName());
    }
}

Main

Counter c1 = new Counter();
Counter c2 = new Counter();

Thread t1 = new Thread(() -> c1.increment());
Thread t2 = new Thread(() -> c2.increment());

Question

Will they block each other?

No. Because
Monitor(c1)≠Monitor(c2)

25.5 Static Synchronized Example

class Counter {
    public static synchronized void print() {
        System.out.println(Thread.currentThread().getName());
    }
}

Main

Thread t1 = new Thread(Counter::print);
Thread t2 = new Thread(Counter::print);

Question
Can both execute simultaneously?

❌ No.
Because both use
Counter.class Monitor

25.6 Internal Working

Instance Method
public synchronized void increment()

JVM internally does

synchronized(this){

}

Static Method

public static synchronized void print()

JVM internally behaves like

synchronized(Counter.class){

}

This is one of the most important interview answers.

