25.10 Real-World Example

Imagine

ATM-1
ATM-2
ATM-3

Each ATM has its own lock.

This is like

Instance Synchronization

Now imagine

Reserve Bank Server

Only one update is allowed globally.

This is like

Static Synchronization

All ATMs must wait because they share the same class-level resource.

17. Instance vs Static Synchronized

| Feature               | Instance `synchronized` | Static `synchronized`            |
| --------------------- | ----------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| Lock                  | `this`                  | `Class` object (`MyClass.class`) |
| Monitor               | Object Monitor          | Class Monitor                    |
| Shared Across Objects | ❌ No                    | ✅ Yes                            |
| Protects              | Instance data           | Static/class data                |
| Concurrency           | Higher                  | Lower                            |

18. Complete Comparison

| Scenario                                    | Block? |
| ------------------------------------------- | ------ |
| Same object → Instance synchronized         | ✅ Yes  |
| Different objects → Instance synchronized   | ❌ No   |
| Two static synchronized methods             | ✅ Yes  |
| Static synchronized + Instance synchronized | ❌ No   |

